            <div xml:id="d86">

                <pb facs="0184" n="94" sameAs="frus:frus1920v02/pg94"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.152H11/416</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Cuba</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gonzales</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-07-25"><hi rendition="#italic">July 25,
                        1919</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received July 29.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1048</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the Department’s instruction
                    No. 831 dated June 27, 1919,<anchor n="92" xml:id="d86-f1"/> with reference to
                    the proposed arbitration of the McGivney &amp; Rokeby Construction Company’s
                    claim against the Cuban Government, and to my telegram No. 33, dated July 18,
                        1919,<anchor n="92" xml:id="d86-f2"/> I have the honor to transmit, herewith
                    enclosed, the translation of Note No. 96, dated July 10, 1919, from the Cuban
                    State Department, which fully explains the position taken by that Government in
                    this case, and which constitutes the formal reply which was promised and
                    mentioned in my telegram.</p>
                <p>I shall await the Department’s instruction before proceding further in this
                    matter.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William E.
                    Gonzales</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d86-a1.xml" xpointer="d86-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
